oofem.out
Corrosion-induced cracking cylinder (axial slice, eigenstrain on rust ITZ)
NonLinearStatic nsteps 100 contextOutputStep 200 nmodules 2 rtolv 1.e-3 stiffMode 1 manrmsteps 10 maxiter 200 controllmode 1 deltat 1.0 lstype 4 smtype 8
vtkxmllattice primvars 1 1 cellvars 9 138 139 140 156 157 158 52 46 103 tstep_step 1 domain_all cross 1 crossstep 1
gpexportmodule vars 2 46 139 tstep_all
domain 3dLattice
OutputManager tstep_all dofman_output { #@CTL1 }
ncrosssect 3 nmat 3 nbc 3 nic 0 nltf 3 nset 2
latticecs 1 material 1
latticecs 2 material 2
latticecs 3 material 3
# Concrete: combined plasticity + damage. Plasticity gives a finite compressive
# yield surface, so the radial compression around the corroding rebar is
# bounded — pure damage models keep accumulating tensile damage from the
# compression-side strains and unphysically lose stiffness. ft randomised via
# random.dat.
latticeplastdam 1 d 0 talpha 0. calpha 0. e 30.e9 ft 3.e6 fc 30.e6 wf 50.e-6 ahard 1.e-3 randvars 1 800 randgen 1 3
# Steel rebar core (inside R=8mm cylinder): linear elastic, no expansion
latticelinearelastic 2 d 0 talpha 0. calpha 0. em 200.e9 nu 0.3
# Corrosion ITZ (0.1mm shell at R=8mm): steel-stiff in the radial direction
# (`e`), shear-free with the surrounding concrete (`a1` near zero) so the
# layer can expand radially without transmitting shear to the matrix.
# calpha drives the eigenstrain via the StructTemperatureLoad below.
latticelinearelastic 3 d 0 talpha 0. e 200.e9 a1 0.001 calpha 0.5e-4
# CTL1 fully fixed (anchors RBM); CTL2 only locks lateral DOFs so the slice
# can expand axially under the corrosion pressure
BoundaryCondition 1 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 4 1 2 3 4 values 4 0 0 0 0 set 1
BoundaryCondition 2 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 3 2 3 4 values 3 0 0 0 set 2
StructTemperatureLoad 3 loadTimeFunction 2 Components 1 1.0
ConstantFunction 1 f(t) 1.
# Linear ramp of the rust eigenstrain over the simulation
PiecewiseLinFunction 2 nPoints 2 t 2 0. 100. f(t) 2 0. 1.
InterpolatingFunction 3 name random.dat dim 3
Set 1 nodes 1 #@CTL1
Set 2 nodes 1 #@CTL2
#%BEGIN_CHECK%
#NODE number #@CTL1 dof 2 unknown d
#LOADLEVEL
#TIME
#%END_CHECK%
